 "notesHtml": "<p>A <a class=\"part\" href=\"/components/LogicValue\"><img src=\"data/icons/64/LogicValue.webp?v=5455a441\" alt=\"\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" loading=\"lazy\" /><span>Logic Value</span></a> outputs 1 when its input is 0.5 or more and 0 below, so a raw error term through one is already &quot;is the error positive&quot;. The <a class=\"part\" href=\"/components/LogicGateNot\"><img src=\"data/icons/64/LogicGateNot.webp?v=76baa871\" alt=\"\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" loading=\"lazy\" /><span>Logic Gate NOT</span></a> on the second branch of the <a class=\"part\" href=\"/components/Router2\"><img src=\"data/icons/64/Router2.webp?v=149dcc6b\" alt=\"\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" loading=\"lazy\" /><span>Data Router 2</span></a> gives the other half. Feed both into the anti-windup circuit.</p>\n\n",
